    "invariants": [
      "All role predicates, write ordering, bounds, neighbor-prefix calls and failure propagation remain in the original Planner::apply_column_write. Only local accepted-value storage changes.",
      "Sparse entries retain the latest material for each exact y; reads consult those before immutable prior runs. Heights remain in the validated 0..4096 request interval.",
      "The ninth distinct position expands the original once, replays every pending latest value and then writes the new value. Subsequent operations follow the existing dense representation.",
      "Sparse finish streams every original run plus sorted unique point edits in ascending order, skips empty spans, coalesces adjacent equal materials and reverses the final canonical runs. It does not mutate shared mask storage.",
      "Heightmaps still use the original ColumnState::from_runs. The caller still compares canonical run bytes and reuses the prior Arc when unchanged.",
      "No new cache, cross-job references or delayed cleanup; pending edits are scoped to one prefix call. The existing opt-in diagnostic snapshot receives only two finish counts."
    ],
    "risks": [
      "Additional small-buffer lookups and enum branches can outweigh avoided dense work for some write patterns. Whole-region and concurrent results must decide acceptance.",
      "This does not reduce feature count, dependency reach or terrain work. Reduced intermediate allocation must be measured rather than inferred as an equivalent latency reduction."
    ],
